 This install applies to "Legends Of Valour" M-) 1992 US-Gold.

 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad 17 or newer, DIC, RawDIC and The Patcher to be
 in the path. The programs can be found in the WHDLoad package.
 To install from a different drive than DF0: select installation mode Expert.

 The installed program requires 0.5 MB ChipMem and 0.7 MB OtherMem.
 It can be quit by pressing F10 (key can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 The game requires an installed A500 Kickstart 1.3 image.
 The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts" and
 must be named "kick34005.A500". The image can be extracted from a A500 with
 tools like 'GrabKick' or similar which can be found on aminet.
 If the image is of wrong version or altered in any way WHDLoad will quit with
 an appropriate message.
 Additionally the file "kick34005.A500.RTB" must be installed in the same
 directory as the kickstart image. It can be found in the archive
 "util/boot/skick345.lha" on aminet.

 Features:
 ---------
 Use Custom1=1 first to launch character creation.

 Enhanced frame rate (Custom2=1) is enabled by the game icon. It turns on all
 enhancements: faster 3D rendering, game timing that keeps the game speed and
 animations correct at any frame rate, finer turning with the mouse, and
 buttons that act once per click. Set Custom2=0 for the original game.

 Text is no longer drawn in wrong colours on fast CPUs (with any setting).

 The enhancements work with the English, German and French versions. Other
 versions run as the original game. For an installed German or French game,
 copy LegendsOfValour.Slave over LegendsOfValourDe.Slave or
 LegendsOfValourFr.Slave and add the tooltype Custom2=1 to its icon.


 History:
 --------
 version 2.0b (08.11.2026) done by Vesuri:
 - faster 3D rendering, using Fast RAM when available
 - chunky-to-planar conversion by Mikael Kalms
 - game timing that keeps the game speed and animations correct at any frame
   rate
 - finer turning with the mouse
 - buttons act once per click: U-turn and other screens no longer repeat
   while the mouse button is held; walking and turning still repeat
 - closing a screen such as the character screen with a click no longer
   reopens it
 - all enhancements behind one option, Enhanced frame rate (Custom2=1),
   enabled by the game icon
 - enhancements for the English, German and French versions
 - fixed text drawn in wrong colours on fast CPUs (missing blitter waits)
 - memory requirement increased to 0.7 MB OtherMem

 version 1.0 (05.02.05) done by CFou!:
 - initial release
 - 4 versions supported (French, German and 2 English)
 - manual protection ripped
 - Custom1=1 tooltype used to launch character creation (use it first)
 - decrunch flash removed
 - Manual picture added
 - some pretty colored icons added

 Thanks Frank and CAPS Tream for original disk images


